    {
      "text": "Blessed are they that mourn, Matt. 5:4 (3 Ne. 12:4). king was sorry, Matt. 14:9 (Mark 6:26). he went away sorrowful, Matt. 19:22 (Luke 18:23). these are the beginning of sorrows, Matt. 24:8 (Mark 13:8). My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even unto death, Matt. 26:38. ye now therefore have sorrow: but I will see you again, John 16:22 (16:6–22). godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation, 2 Cor. 7:10. sorrow not, even as others which have no hope, 1 Thes. 4:13. they have erred from the faith, and pierced themselves through with many sorrows, 1 Tim. 6:10. there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, Rev. 21:4 (D&C 101:29).",
